/**
 * @defgroup FpdmGeo FpdmGeo — Forward Pion Detector / FMS Geometry
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief AGML geometry definitions for the STAR Forward Pion Detector (FPD) and
 *        Forward Meson Spectrometer (FMS)
 *
 * @details
 * The FpdmGeo package (detector tag **FPDM**) describes the evolution of the STAR
 * forward lead-glass calorimeter system from the original eight-module Forward Pion
 * Detector (FPD, Run 2003–2005) to the large-aperture Forward Meson Spectrometer
 * (FMS, Run 2006+).  These detectors measure neutral pions, η mesons, and direct
 * photons at forward rapidity (η ≈ 2.5–4) via the Cherenkov light they produce in
 * lead-glass crystals.
 *
 * ### Lead-glass crystal properties
 * All versions use Protovino-type (IHEP) lead-glass with composition Pb/K/Si/O/As,
 * density 3.86 g/cm³, and radiation length 2.5 cm.  Crystals are 3.81 cm × 3.81 cm × 45 cm
 * (~18 X₀ deep).  The FMS west large-cell array uses Fermilab Lab (FLab) type crystals
 * at 5.812 cm × 5.812 cm × 45 cm.  Each crystal is wrapped in 10 μm of aluminium and
 * read out via a photo-cathode tube (FPCT) behind a μ-metal shield (FUMT).
 *
 * ### FPD configuration (FpdmGeo1–2)
 * Eight modules are distributed symmetrically around the interaction point: four on the
 * east side (EN, ES, ET, EB) and four on the west (WN, WS, WT, WB).  North/south
 * modules (type 1) are 7×7 crystal arrays with a preshower lead plate (PBPT) and a
 * two-plane scintillator-strip shower-maximum detector (FSHM/FHMS, 50 strips per plane).
 * Top/bottom modules (type 2) are bare 5×5 arrays.
 *
 * ### FMS configuration (FpdmGeo3–4)
 * The west modules are replaced by two large half-wheel arrays (north and south) each
 * containing a 17×34 large-cell + 12×24 small-cell sub-array arranged side-by-side in x.
 * The default x-positions (`FmsNorthX`, `FmsSouthX`) are adjustable via the FMCG
 * structure, enabling the "open position" survey configuration (FPDM13).
 *
 * FpdmGeo4 adds a forward pre-shower (FPS) comprising scintillator panels (PRSW, POST)
 * upstream of the FMS, and a west-platform iron support structure (WPFM).
 *
 * ### Cherenkov simulation
 * When `FMCG.ChkvSim = 1`, the GSCKOV optical-photon simulation is activated for the
 * lead-glass (FLGR), aluminium wrapper (FWAL), photo-cathode (FPCT), silicon rubber
 * (SiRub), and μ-metal (FUMT) media with tabulated refractive indices, absorption
 * lengths, and photo-cathode efficiencies.  The default (`ChkvSim = 0`) records
 * ionisation energy loss only.
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @file FpdmGeo1.xml
 * @brief Module FPDMGEO1 — FPD version 6.0, symmetric 8-module layout (Ogawa 2003).
 *
 * Defines 8 FPOS entries (iMod = 1–8) for EN, ES, ET, EB (east, z ≈ −590/−752 cm) and
 * WN, WS, WT, WB (west, z ≈ +590/+752 cm).  Module type 1 = 7×7 + SMD + preshower;
 * type 2 = 5×5.  SMD strips defined by FMXG: 50 triangular strips, apex 0.7 cm, base
 * 1.0 cm, G10 substrate 0.15 cm thick.
 */

/**
 * @file FpdmGeo2.xml
 * @brief Module FPDMGEO2 — FPD/FMS transition geometry version 7.0.
 *
 * Replaces west modules (WN, WS) with type-3 14×14+6×6 combined arrays at z = 700 cm.
 * Adds `PbPlate` switch to FMCG to toggle the preshower lead plate.
 * FBXD type 3 defines the combined west module geometry.
 */

/**
 * @file FpdmGeo3.xml
 * @brief Module FPDMGEO3 — FMS geometry version 8.0 (2006+).
 *
 * Consolidates to 4 modules: east EN/ES (7×7, iType=1), west WN/WS (17×34+14×28, iType=2).
 * Introduces `INSE` structure for FMS insertion geometry, `FmsNorthX`/`FmsSouthX`
 * parameters for x-positioning, and `atten` switch for light-attenuation correction.
 * FPDM13 uses extreme x-offsets (±50.3 cm) to model the detector in the open position.
 */

/**
 * @file FpdmGeo4.xml
 * @brief Module FPDMGEO4 — FMS + Forward Pre-Shower geometry version 9.0.
 *
 * Adds three structures beyond FpdmGeo3:
 * - **PRSW** — forward pre-shower panel geometry (scintillator strips before FMS)
 * - **POST** — post-shower layer geometry
 * - **WPFM** — iron west-platform support (pole, I-beam, U-beam structures)
 *
 * The `postshower` flag in FMCG (default 0) activates the POST layer when set to 1
 * (FPDMv4, FPDMv4at setups).
 */

/**
 * @file FpdmConfig.xml
 * @brief Setup registry for detector FPDM.
 *
 * | Setup | Module | Notes |
 * |---|---|---|
 * | FPDMof | FpdmGeo1 | disabled |
 * | FPDM00/01 | FpdmGeo1 | FPD 8-module |
 * | FPDM02 | FpdmGeo2 | FPD+FMS transition |
 * | FPDM03 | FpdmGeo3 | FMS default position |
 * | FPDM03at | FpdmGeo3 | FMS + attenuation |
 * | FPDM04 | FpdmGeo4 | FMS + FPS |
 * | FPDM04at | FpdmGeo4 | FMS + FPS + attenuation |
 * | FPDMv4 | FpdmGeo4 | FMS + FPS + post-shower |
 * | FPDMv4at | FpdmGeo4 | FMS + FPS + post-shower + attenuation |
 * | FPDM13 | FpdmGeo3 | FMS open-position survey |
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
